that I am married to work.

262
00:19:58.989 --> 00:20:01.074
I am not interested in men...

263
00:20:04.745 --> 00:20:05.579
at all

264
00:20:13.503 --> 00:20:16.173
Marry even a job, even a pillow.

265
00:20:16.256 --> 00:20:17.424
How does this apply to me?

266
00:20:18.050 --> 00:20:19.718
If you share personal information,

267
00:20:19.801 --> 00:20:21.637
then it's better to say the bank password.

268
00:20:24.806 --> 00:20:27.267
Didn't we sometimes go to school together?

269
00:20:27.351 --> 00:20:29.519
- Very unlikely.
- Have we met?

270
00:20:31.980 --> 00:20:33.190
Then you would remember me.

271
00:20:33.273 --> 00:20:35.692
You are not my school friend or ex.

272
00:20:36.735 --> 00:20:38.111
Where are your manners?

273
00:20:39.154 --> 00:20:41.198
For me, everyone is a person

274
00:20:42.282 --> 00:20:43.408
equally unimportant.

275
00:20:44.534 --> 00:20:46.662
<i>What's the matter with this beautiful madman?</i>

276
00:20:55.545 --> 00:20:57.172
<i>I'm keeping my end of the bargain.</i>

277
00:20:57.256 --> 00:20:58.548
<i>I hope you do too.</i>

278
00:20:58.632 --> 00:20:59.758
Almighty

279
00:21:00.342 --> 00:21:02.761
Why should I endure these hardships?

280
00:21:04.471 --> 00:21:05.305
30 MINUTES

281
00:21:05.389 --> 00:21:06.223
START

282
00:21:12.604 --> 00:21:15.857
I booked this whole restaurant
to eat in peace.

283
00:21:15.941 --> 00:21:16.817
Sounds good.

284
00:21:16.900 --> 00:21:18.110
It will be cute and awkward.

285
00:21:18.944 --> 00:21:21.238
If you want to eat, there are other restaurants.

286
00:21:21.321 --> 00:21:23.782
Then you go.
You definitely know a lot of establishments.

287
00:21:26.243 --> 00:21:28.287
<i>What's with this crazy madwoman?</i>

288
00:21:35.961 --> 00:21:36.795
Give

289
00:21:39.339 --> 00:21:40.716
I want two of them.

290
00:21:41.216 --> 00:21:44.594
And me too
your strongest wine, please.

291
00:21:44.678 --> 00:21:45.512
Of course, sir.

292
00:21:48.181 --> 00:21:49.057
Steak with garlic…

293
00:21:49.933 --> 00:21:51.310
"To To Hee."

294
00:21:51.393 --> 00:21:53.228
Myers - Briggs Type: ISTJ.

295
00:21:53.312 --> 00:21:55.022
Probably, she is not capable of empathy.

296
00:21:55.105 --> 00:21:58.525
LOST PARENTS AT THE AGE OF 11 YEARS,
ADOPTED BY CHAIRMAN OF MIRE GROUP CHU

297
00:22:05.824 --> 00:22:07.659
Who is he, child?

298
00:22:10.829 --> 00:22:12.497
I enjoyed your youthful spirit.

299
00:22:14.416 --> 00:22:16.543
I really look
much younger than her age.

300
00:22:17.502 --> 00:22:20.505
You definitely did not want to eat, then explain to me.

301
00:22:20.589 --> 00:22:22.632
why do you insist
to stay?

302
00:22:22.716 --> 00:22:25.052
I'm going to stay
30 minutes as a courtesy.

303
00:22:25.135 --> 00:22:26.094
Courtesy to whom?

304
00:22:26.178 --> 00:22:28.263
It's incredibly rude of you to stay.

305
00:22:29.181 --> 00:22:30.557
I am like a mirror.

306
00:22:30.640 --> 00:22:32.893
I repel your rude behavior.

307
00:22:36.813 --> 00:22:39.107
You have to come up with an excuse
why didn't it work

308
00:22:39.691 --> 00:22:40.609
Why not say…

309
00:22:41.735 --> 00:22:43.779
that you were frightened by my beauty?

310
00:22:44.321 --> 00:22:45.947
Why are you doing this to me?

311
00:22:46.031 --> 00:22:47.491
I don't want to do that.

312
00:22:47.574 --> 00:22:49.284
I'm just following orders from above.

313
00:22:50.410 --> 00:22:51.328
"Above"?

314
00:22:51.411 --> 00:22:54.790
I dare not disobey
order of our Almighty power.

315
00:22:58.293 --> 00:22:59.878
Who the hell are you…

316
00:23:00.670 --> 00:23:01.588
That is, who are you?

317
00:23:01.671 --> 00:23:02.506
I almost forgot.

318
00:23:03.006 --> 00:23:05.050
We have to recommend ourselves properly.

319
00:23:07.302 --> 00:23:08.220
CEO TO TO HI

320
00:23:09.679 --> 00:23:10.722
"To To Hee"?

321
00:23:16.144 --> 00:23:17.312
Give me yours.

322
00:23:17.896 --> 00:23:20.398
unlike you
I do not share personal information.

323
00:23:20.482 --> 00:23:23.110
I understand that you were forced to be here
just like me

324
00:23:23.193 --> 00:23:26.029
but to overcome it, we have to cooperate.

325
00:23:35.038 --> 00:23:36.540
"Jeong Koo Won".

326
00:23:37.290 --> 00:23:40.127
Translated "salvation"? It doesn't suit you at all.

327
00:23:41.378 --> 00:23:43.046
"Sunwol Foundation"?

328
00:23:43.130 --> 00:23:44.548
A familiar name.

329
00:23:44.631 --> 00:23:48.468
My foundation supports traditional artists,
such as traditional singers and dancers,

330
00:23:48.552 --> 00:23:50.595
produces regularly
great traditional performances.

331
00:23:50.679 --> 00:23:52.556
How do you not know such a well-known organization?

332
00:23:53.765 --> 00:23:55.559
Shouldn't you be a bit more cultured?

333
00:23:55.642 --> 00:23:57.644
The tradition…

334
00:23:57.727 --> 00:23:58.854
I only hear about her.

335
00:23:58.937 --> 00:24:00.772
I'm not against tradition

336
00:24:00.856 --> 00:24:03.358
but my life
rather like modern warfare,

337
00:24:03.441 --> 00:24:06.069
than for a concert in a traditional pavilion.

338
00:24:06.153 --> 00:24:07.904
So what is the sacred plan?

339
00:24:07.988 --> 00:24:08.989
don't say

340
00:24:09.781 --> 00:24:11.616
that you were dragged into it without details.

341
00:24:14.119 --> 00:24:15.704
This is really a blind date.

342
00:24:15.787 --> 00:24:16.621
Date?

343
00:24:16.705 --> 00:24:18.540
Probably, you are not a gift either,

344
00:24:18.623 --> 00:24:20.667
if you were tricked into being here.

345
00:24:20.750 --> 00:24:24.254
So what exactly is going on here?

346
00:24:25.130 --> 00:24:26.173
A blind date.

347
00:24:26.256 --> 00:24:27.883
We were forced to meet.

348
00:24:28.800 --> 00:24:30.427
you say

349
00:24:30.510 --> 00:24:34.055
that God made me meet you?

350
00:24:36.766 --> 00:24:38.977
Calling her God is already too much

351
00:24:39.060 --> 00:24:41.938
even for the second half
of our Almighty Chu.

352
00:24:42.606 --> 00:24:44.024
"Almighty Chu"?

353
00:24:44.649 --> 00:24:47.444
So who did you call "Almighty"?

354
00:24:56.870 --> 00:24:58.288
You must be in shock.

355
00:24:58.872 --> 00:24:59.915
Interesting.

356
00:24:59.998 --> 00:25:02.334
No person has ever confused me like that.

357
00:25:02.417 --> 00:25:04.753
Glad at least one of us enjoyed it.

358
00:25:06.922 --> 00:25:08.632
Sorry, we are busy.

359
00:25:08.715 --> 00:25:10.342
Sorry to spoil the fun

360
00:25:10.926 --> 00:25:12.886
but Cinderella's time is up. Be there.

361
00:25:40.288 --> 00:25:41.831
<i>Cold, but kind.</i>

362
00:25:41.915 --> 00:25:43.333
<i>Innocent but sexy.</i>

363
00:25:43.959 --> 00:25:47.379
<i>His whole being is permeated with sensuality.</i>

364
00:25:51.383 --> 00:25:52.634
It was dangerous.

365
00:25:56.179 --> 00:25:57.973
Sorry. I'll be right back.

366
00:26:01.351 --> 00:26:02.978
My expensive cake was almost ruined.

367
00:26:17.993 --> 00:26:19.077
What was it?

368
00:26:19.828 --> 00:26:21.538
Maybe he's not such a scoundrel after all.

369
00:26:21.621 --> 00:26:23.665
He even cooked for me
birthday cake?

370
00:26:31.548 --> 00:26:32.549
Devil.

371
00:26:47.564 --> 00:26:48.815
Little scoundrel!

372
00:26:48.898 --> 00:26:50.150
Who sent you

373
00:26:50.233 --> 00:26:51.901
What did you do to our boss?

374
00:26:51.985 --> 00:26:53.737
hold on

375
00:26:54.904 --> 00:26:57.157
I reserved the restaurant a month ago

376
00:26:57.240 --> 00:26:59.284
and sat through a boring meal for the sake of it.

377
00:26:59.367 --> 00:27:01.202
So let me taste it first.

378
00:27:22.098 --> 00:27:24.017
Does not wash off.

379
00:27:28.897 --> 00:27:31.733
But how could he
so flirting without warning?

380
00:27:33.526 --> 00:27:34.611
Was he evasive?

381
00:27:35.111 --> 00:27:36.905
It was dangerous.

382
00:27:40.492 --> 00:27:41.951
I should have been more careful.

383
00:27:42.577 --> 00:27:46.164
Probably let her charm shine
without noticing it herself.

384
00:27:47.082 --> 00:27:50.627
Am I the first woman who has embarrassed him so much?

385
00:27:50.710 --> 00:27:54.297
No person has ever confused me like that.

386
00:27:58.760 --> 00:27:59.844
What is it?

387
00:27:59.928 --> 00:28:02.222
It can't be. Am I fumbling?

388
00:28:02.305 --> 00:28:03.515
The whole face turned red!

389
00:28:03.598 --> 00:28:04.641
What is it?

390
00:28:04.724 --> 00:28:06.184
Get a grip, To To Hee.

391
00:28:06.267 --> 00:28:07.519
The name means "proud".

392
00:28:07.602 --> 00:28:08.895
This is not your first time.

393
00:28:10.355 --> 00:28:12.482
There are different types of garbage.

394
00:28:12.565 --> 00:28:13.775
Which one do you belong to?

395
00:28:14.401 --> 00:28:16.861
Garbage for recycling? Food?

396
00:28:16.945 --> 00:28:18.988
Don't you understand what's going on here?

397
00:28:19.489 --> 00:28:21.324
It doesn't look like I can remake you

398
00:28:21.408 --> 00:28:23.410
and I don't think you are nutritious.

399
00:28:25.370 --> 00:28:26.871
That is, you are ordinary garbage.

400
00:28:31.042 --> 00:28:32.001
Beat him up.

401
00:28:45.849 --> 00:28:47.809
- What the hell?
- What happened?

402
00:28:47.892 --> 00:28:49.352
Where did he disappear to?

403
00:28:49.436 --> 00:28:50.562
You try.

404
00:28:51.938 --> 00:28:53.773
{\an8}IT IS NEVER TOO LATE FOR YOUR HAIR!

405
00:29:01.781 --> 00:29:04.576
ACT BEFORE YOU LOSE
EVEN MORE HAIR

406
00:29:07.746 --> 00:29:09.706
- Hold on.
- Just a minute.

407
00:29:09.789 --> 00:29:11.082
We must attack together.

408
00:29:11.166 --> 00:29:13.001
Devil. Let's try.

409
00:29:20.508 --> 00:29:22.177
hold on

410
00:29:31.311 --> 00:29:32.145
Oh no!

411
00:29:49.120 --> 00:29:50.038
Interesting.

412
00:29:50.121 --> 00:29:52.457
Windbag! Zombie!

413
00:29:52.540 --> 00:29:53.750
Time to push.

414
00:29:54.334 --> 00:29:57.504
What is going on here? what are you doing

415
00:29:57.587 --> 00:29:59.088
Don't you see?

416
00:29:59.172 --> 00:30:00.089
I clean

417
00:30:00.173 --> 00:30:02.717
Ordinary garbage is buried or burned.

418
00:30:02.801 --> 00:30:05.637
What should I do with you three?

419
00:30:06.262 --> 00:30:07.180
Well, because

420
00:30:07.680 --> 00:30:08.723
Ah, you are little...

421
00:30:09.474 --> 00:30:11.726
Don't do it!

422
00:30:13.561 --> 00:30:14.813
Oh, don't stop me.

423
00:30:23.571 --> 00:30:27.116
I've been so busy lately
work that has not been seen for a long time.

424
00:30:32.956 --> 00:30:35.041
Why do I touch up lipstick?

425
00:30:35.124 --> 00:30:37.585
What am I waiting for?

426
00:30:37.669 --> 00:30:38.628
I must be crazy.

427
00:30:38.711 --> 00:30:40.421
Put it back.

428
00:30:42.215 --> 00:30:43.049
Again?

429
00:30:44.467 --> 00:30:47.095
How dare they screw it up
my precious dessert time?

430
00:30:49.973 --> 00:30:52.767
No matter how busy I am,
it will be rude to leave without tasting...

431
00:30:53.560 --> 00:30:54.394
a cake

432
00:30:56.104 --> 00:30:57.230
The party is over.

433
00:30:57.313 --> 00:30:58.189
Did you complete it yourself?

434
00:30:58.273 --> 00:31:01.025
People eat alone all the time.
Can't I celebrate by myself?

435
00:31:01.651 --> 00:31:04.779
- How could you eat a cake on my day...
- Who said he is yours?

436
00:31:04.863 --> 00:31:06.656
What do I care about your birthday?

437
00:31:08.533 --> 00:31:10.159
So go ahead.

438
00:31:10.243 --> 00:31:13.288
I'm too preoccupied with trash
to deal with you.

439
00:31:17.166 --> 00:31:18.543
It was nice to meet you.

440
00:31:18.626 --> 00:31:20.837
I hope your day continues to be awful.

441
00:31:21.671 --> 00:31:22.589
And something else.

442
00:31:23.464 --> 00:31:25.925
speak politely
if we ever meet again

443
00:31:26.009 --> 00:31:28.011
I don't want them to think you're my ex.

444
00:31:30.138 --> 00:31:32.056
Shouldn't you ask more politely?

445
00:31:32.140 --> 00:31:33.016
I didn't even ask.

446
00:31:38.605 --> 00:31:40.523
{\an8}CAFE "PLACE OF ESCAPE": CLOSE
HOW IS IT DOWN THERE?

447
00:31:46.112 --> 00:31:46.946
Yes.

448
00:31:51.034 --> 00:31:53.077
VISIT THE WORST PRISON
NEW HISTORY

449
00:32:07.884 --> 00:32:08.885
It's me!

450
00:32:09.761 --> 00:32:11.804
- Move!
- Be careful, boss.

451
00:32:11.888 --> 00:32:14.599
My hand!

452
00:32:14.682 --> 00:32:16.017
Seriously!

453
00:32:22.982 --> 00:32:25.693
How could Ms. Chu
set me up with such a scoundrel?

454
00:32:27.320 --> 00:32:29.405
Did you find out who is behind that article?

455
00:32:30.239 --> 00:32:32.867
As you said
it was an attempt to seize power from within.

456
00:32:34.661 --> 00:32:35.954
Who was it?

457
00:32:36.037 --> 00:32:37.580
Ms. No Soo Ahn of Mire Clothing.

458
00:32:38.164 --> 00:32:39.874
She was recently at a fashion show

459
00:32:39.958 --> 00:32:42.502
and made friends with the head
news agency where the article appeared.

460
00:32:42.585 --> 00:32:46.297
Why won't they give me peace
when I just want to live peacefully?

461
00:32:52.428 --> 00:32:54.889
"MIRE GROUP"

462
00:32:55.682 --> 00:32:58.434
<i>Mire Group, one of ten
of the best companies in the country,</i>

463
00:32:58.518 --> 00:33:00.395
<i>experiences an internal struggle for power.</i>

464
00:33:02.855 --> 00:33:05.608
<i>"Kingdom of Mire"
founded by Almighty Chu,</i>

465
00:33:06.275 --> 00:33:07.443
<i>chairman Choo Jeong-suk.</i>

466
00:33:09.153 --> 00:33:11.447
<i>I call her Ms. Chu.</i>

467
00:33:12.865 --> 00:33:15.785
A YEAR AGO

468
00:33:17.495 --> 00:33:18.830
HAPPY BIRTHDAY MOM

469
00:33:18.913 --> 00:33:21.082
HEAD OF "MIRE GROUP"
CHU CHONG SUK

470
00:33:22.667 --> 00:33:24.419
I wish you many years of health, mother.

471
00:33:24.502 --> 00:33:25.586
Don't worry.

472
00:33:25.670 --> 00:33:26.921
I will survive you.

473
00:33:27.005 --> 00:33:28.256
I hope so.

474
00:33:28.339 --> 00:33:30.091
<i>No Suk Min, the eldest son of Mrs. Choo.</i>

475
00:33:30.174 --> 00:33:33.511
<i>Poor heir to the throne,
who is forever in the shadow of his mother.</i>

476
00:33:33.594 --> 00:33:35.638
Still drinking like a chip?

477
00:33:35.722 --> 00:33:37.807
I haven't had a drink in over ten years, Mom.

478
00:33:39.225 --> 00:33:41.936
You look especially pretty today, Mom.

479
00:33:42.020 --> 00:33:43.479
<i>Kim Se La, daughter-in-law.</i>

480
00:33:43.563 --> 00:33:45.898
<i>Elegant peacock, eternally hungry for approval.</i>

481
00:33:45.982 --> 00:33:47.400
Have you had facial surgery?

482
00:33:47.483 --> 00:33:49.318
Of course not.

483
00:33:49.402 --> 00:33:51.904
I just hung on
for a special day.

484
00:33:51.988 --> 00:33:53.448
Think about it.

485
00:33:57.952 --> 00:33:59.787
<i>No To Kyung, the couple's only son.</i>

486
00:33:59.871 --> 00:34:02.540
<i>He learned to be invisible in order to survive.</i>

487
00:34:02.623 --> 00:34:04.876
Mom

488
00:34:04.959 --> 00:34:06.961
Happy birthday, mom.

489
00:34:07.045 --> 00:34:09.047
<i>No Su An, Mrs. Chu's second child.</i>

490
00:34:09.130 --> 00:34:12.175
<i>She is so fond of Paris,
pretending to live there.</i>

491
00:34:12.258 --> 00:34:14.177
<i>She is called Parisu-an.</i>

492
00:34:14.260 --> 00:34:16.679
<i>Austin and Justin are her twin sons</i>

493
00:34:16.763 --> 00:34:18.056
<i>born one minute apart.</i>

494
00:34:18.139 --> 00:34:21.100
- Grandma, happy birthday.
- Grandma, happy birthday.

495
00:34:22.226 --> 00:34:24.562
What a bunch of international delusion.

496
00:34:25.146 --> 00:34:28.191
My husband could not come
through the scientific publication schedule.

497
00:34:28.274 --> 00:34:30.526
He is very sorry that he could not come.

498
00:34:30.610 --> 00:34:33.237
But he already gave me a present.

499
00:34:34.447 --> 00:34:36.199
without coming

500
00:34:38.910 --> 00:34:41.704
{\an8}<i>Su An's husband -
a professor at the Ivy League University.</i>

501
00:34:41.788 --> 00:34:44.624
{\an8}<i>He is called the Unicorn,
so rarely does he appear.</i>

502
00:34:45.249 --> 00:34:47.001
<i>Chu Seok-hoon, Mrs. Chu's nephew.</i>

503
00:34:47.085 --> 00:34:48.711
Happy birthday, Aunt Jung Suk.

504
00:34:48.795 --> 00:34:50.755
You look neat as always.

505
00:34:51.589 --> 00:34:54.217
Well, I'm too busy
increasing your wealth.

506
00:34:54.300 --> 00:34:55.760
<i>Although besides him there is no more Chu,</i>

507
00:34:55.843 --> 00:34:58.721
<i>he is only a business partner for Ms. Chu.</i>

508
00:34:58.805 --> 00:35:01.682
Are your parents still in Mongolia or something?

509
00:35:02.183 --> 00:35:03.017
They are in Peru.

510
00:35:03.893 --> 00:35:05.853
<i>- You are a year older, sister.
- Seok Hoon's father...</i>

511
00:35:05.937 --> 00:35:07.980
<i>- Happy birthday.
- ...younger brother Jung Suk.</i>

512
00:35:08.064 --> 00:35:10.066
<i>- Go to retirement...
- He and his wife are thrifty hippies

513
00:35:10.149 --> 00:35:11.901
<i>- ...and travel like us.</i>
- Do they even wash themselves?

514
00:35:11.984 --> 00:35:14.654
- They are indistinguishable from alpacas.
<i>- Happy birthday.</i>

515
00:35:16.739 --> 00:35:19.200
If everyone has come, are you ready for pictures?

516
00:35:21.285 --> 00:35:22.286
Where is To Hee?

517
00:35:23.913 --> 00:35:25.081
Probably late.

518
00:35:25.581 --> 00:35:28.167
The whole family is equally here.
Let's just take a picture.

519
00:35:28.251 --> 00:35:29.210
Yes, mom.

520
00:35:29.293 --> 00:35:30.461
Chasu katma.

521
00:35:30.545 --> 00:35:31.379
leave it

522
00:35:31.462 --> 00:35:33.172
I won't take a picture without To Hee.

523
00:35:34.674 --> 00:35:37.176
